[00:00.000] 作词 : Austin Lunn
[00:01.000] 作曲 : Austin Lunn
[00:39.481]The firelight flickers against my withered, weathered hands
[01:07.792]The years reflected in the dancing flame
[01:36.708]Grey as the ash I am
[01:48.694]Resisting, resisting the change
[02:01.163]In my last days
[02:05.707]Through many winters I have become
[02:17.997]Until I realized that I became
[03:22.337]The rustling leaves and falling snow
[03:36.388]My name again no one will know
[03:58.628]Whose land did I wander before I tread here?
[04:16.332]Whose forests were ever white?
[04:26.984]Whose firelight warmed my frozen fingers
[04:41.122]Whose emerald green blazed the night?
[05:23.437]What of blind folds and tattered banners?
[05:37.783]Or father’s gods or mother’s cross?
[05:51.990]The empty rooms adorned in cobwebs
[06:06.149]Life in solitude’s accounted cost.
[06:20.431]My cabin ruins let in the winter
[06:34.421]My poems’ words of grief and loss.
[06:48.888]My poems’ words of grief and loss.
[07:34.851]Through many winters I have become
[07:48.215]Until I realized that I became
[08:02.385]The rustling leaves and falling snow
[08:16.588]My name again no one will know
[08:30.685]My name again no one will know
[08:44.802]My name again no one will know
[08:58.991]The ghostly figure behind me
[09:06.990]only the flickering of candle flame
[09:13.437]whose breath is the smoke of the burning wick
[09:20.480]whose sigh is the echo of the clock tick
[09:27.546]concerned ever less than I should be
[09:34.635]for the dwindling wood for the evening fire
[09:41.636]for the barren shelves in the cupboard remain
[09:48.910]minute by minute
[09:51.877]watching the clock expire
[09:55.063](awaiting) As the cedar withers and cracks
[10:01.096](awaiting) As the winter loosens its grasp
[10:08.405]As the caribou draws its final breath
[10:15.432]As the rice grows soon upon the shore line
[10:22.243] (awaiting) As the cedar withers and cracks
[10:29.462](awaiting) As the winter loosens its grasp
[10:36.842]As the caribou draws its final breath
[10:43.982]As the rice grows soon upon the shore line
[10:50.987](awaiting) As the cedar withers and cracks
[10:57.907](awaiting) As the winter loosens its grasp
[11:05.312]As the caribou draws its final breath
[11:12.376]As the rice grows soon upon the shore line
[11:19.343](awaiting) As the cedar withers and cracks
[11:26.379](awaiting) As the winter loosens its grasp
[11:33.717]As the caribou draws its final breath
[11:40.803]As the rice grows soon upon the shore line
[11:49.459]I’ll remain on this land and I await my death.
